WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.552 --> 00:00:01.760
- Hey what can I get you?

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:03.430
Our house coffee is four hours old

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.598
and I just had a panic attack
in our walk-in freezer.

00:00:05.598 --> 00:00:06.623
(whoosh)

00:00:06.623 --> 00:00:07.646
(Cranking sound)

00:00:07.646 --> 00:00:11.582
(folky country music)

00:00:11.582 --> 00:00:12.666
- I saw you didn't use the tip jar

00:00:12.666 --> 00:00:15.086
so I'm gonna grab your
muffin with my bare hands.

00:00:15.086 --> 00:00:17.707
- This milk expired two days ago

00:00:17.707 --> 00:00:20.084
but if I add some chocolate
you really won't notice

00:00:20.084 --> 00:00:21.127
the difference.

00:00:21.127 --> 00:00:22.129
- Oh.

00:00:22.129 --> 00:00:23.129
(laughing)

00:00:23.129 --> 00:00:24.630
I'm laughing to cover up how
badly I just burned myself.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.779
(ice crackling)

00:00:26.779 --> 00:00:27.748
- Which coffee is my favorite?

00:00:27.748 --> 00:00:29.452
Well the single origin is nice and fruity

00:00:29.452 --> 00:00:31.460
and the house blend tastes
like a chemical fire.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.796
(wooshing)

00:00:32.796 --> 00:00:34.674
- Oh you didn't actually
say you wanted it iced

00:00:34.674 --> 00:00:35.850
but that's no problem.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.494
I'll just remake it and
put my fingers in it.

00:00:38.494 --> 00:00:41.090
- A flavored latte is pretty
much just a milkshake.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:42.692
And if you get whipped cream on it,

00:00:42.692 --> 00:00:44.231
it's a (bleeping) milkshake.

00:00:44.231 --> 00:00:45.935
- I'm only smiling because my face muscles

00:00:45.935 --> 00:00:48.225
are so full of caffeine
that if I relax them

00:00:48.225 --> 00:00:50.506
my heart might explode.

00:00:50.506 --> 00:00:51.608
(stirring liquid)

00:00:51.608 --> 00:00:52.612
(market writing on paper)

00:00:52.612 --> 00:00:53.610
- Kim.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.443
P-O-L-F.

00:00:56.744 --> 00:00:58.334
Thanks.

00:00:58.334 --> 00:00:59.338
- Is our coffee strong?

00:00:59.338 --> 00:01:00.819
Well I haven't slept for days

00:01:00.819 --> 00:01:03.167
and I feel like I'm in a waking nightmare.

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:05.473
- I actually really like
waking up early for this job.

00:01:05.473 --> 00:01:07.923
Let's make it a fork at two
p.m. so I can immediately

00:01:07.923 --> 00:01:09.185
start day drinking.

00:01:09.185 --> 00:01:11.041
- Quadruple latte with half and half?

00:01:11.041 --> 00:01:12.459
Enjoy shitting your pants.

00:01:12.459 --> 00:01:14.261
- You seem like an asshole
so I'm gonna give you the

00:01:14.261 --> 00:01:15.421
smallest croissant.

00:01:15.421 --> 00:01:17.424
It's the one thing in my
life that I can control.

00:01:17.424 --> 00:01:18.458
(spraying)

00:01:18.458 --> 00:01:19.452
(pouring)

00:01:19.452 --> 00:01:20.454
(wiping)

00:01:20.454 --> 00:01:21.642
- You want that cappuccino extra hot?

00:01:21.642 --> 00:01:24.548
It's gonna burn your (bleeping) face off.

00:01:24.548 --> 00:01:26.817
- One cup of sugar syrup for Polf?

00:01:26.817 --> 00:01:27.977
- I know I serve you every morning

00:01:27.977 --> 00:01:29.569
but if I see you in public

00:01:29.569 --> 00:01:31.142
I'm gonna run the opposite direction.

00:01:31.142 --> 00:01:32.146
- How am I doing?

00:01:32.146 --> 00:01:33.616
I'm hoping to replace this hangover

00:01:33.616 --> 00:01:35.614
with enough coffee to
jumpstart a dump truck.

00:01:35.614 --> 00:01:36.624
- Thanks for ordering tea.

00:01:36.624 --> 00:01:38.838
It's something you probably
should've made at home.

00:01:38.838 --> 00:01:40.798
- This isn't what you
ordered but I'm gonna call

00:01:40.798 --> 00:01:43.492
your name anyway 'cause I
really don't give a (bleeping).

00:01:43.492 --> 00:01:46.659
(folky country music)

